Source of include/PR/*.h and include/ultra64.h
  Open reconstruction: decompals/ultralib (https://github.com/decompals/ultralib), include/PR and include/ultra64.h,
  commit e24c836796df4bf520ff8b11a5c9d2cea3a66cbd (2026-04-19). Files keep their SGI names, paths and macro names.
  Nothing was copied from the leaked SDK.
Deviation from the ultralib text
  ultratypes.h: u32 is unsigned int and s32 is int (ultralib: unsigned long / long), as in BattleTanx 35dbea7 and as
  the project's own TYPES.H has always typedef'd them. The matched libultra objects (sdk/libultra/os/sendmesg.c,
  recvmesg.c, jammesg.c, osyieldthread.CPP) were matched with int-sized s32/u32; vu32/vs32 stay long.
  ultratypes.h: _MIPS_SZLONG tests are guarded with defined(); the SN gcc 2.8.1 preprocessor (-undef) does not define it,
  and the default is the 32-bit long case.
  R4300.h: the include guard is __R4300_H__ and it includes <PR/ultratypes.h> (the project's own copy had the same).
  libaudio.h: the tempo argument of alSeqTicksToSec, alCSeqTicksToSec and alCSeqSecToTicks is s32 (ultralib: u32). The matched
  bodies in sdk/libultra/audio/seq.c (alSeqTicksToSec) and cseq.c (alCSeqTicksToSec, alCSeqSecToTicks) convert the signed
  tempo to f64 and add the unsigned bias by hand; with u32 the compiler emits a different conversion.
  os_thread.h: __OSThreadContext also holds fp1, fp3 .. fp31 after fp30 (sizeof(OSThread) 560, ultralib 432), as the
  game's own type records in src/DATA/OVERLAYS/ELEVEN/CONSTANTS/G_DEBUGSTREAMHALFWORDS1.CPP list them (fp1 at 400). The
  matched OSSched users (sdk/libultra/sched/sched_handleretrace.CPP, sched_runeventloop.CPP) read fields behind thread.
  sptask.h, sched.h: OSTask's force_structure_alignment is u32[2] (ultralib: long long) and OSScTask
  startTime/totalTime (OSScTime) are unsigned long long aligned to 4, so struct Frame in include/COMMON/DISPLAY.H is 4-aligned, sizeof(Display) is 0x3C4 and the GameSession members
  follow it at their ROM offsets; SetN64_AdvanceDisplayFrame (src/ENGINE/SETN64/SETN64_ADVANCEDISPLAYFRAME.CPP) loads
  ring.current with lw, not ulw.
  sched.h: OSSched holds prenmiMsg before retraceMsg (ultralib: retraceMsg first); the matched
  sdk/libultra/sched/sched_handleretrace.CPP, sched_runeventloop.CPP and sched_runeventloopus.CPP send &sc->retraceMsg at +32.
Compiler flags
  -D_LANGUAGE_C (config.toml cppflags) selects the C declarations in the PR headers; no other flag was added.
